sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-glue-13> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-13--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-13--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on levin-2023-glue-13: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.45" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.45"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.58"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The dissociation among current anatomy, voltage pattern, expression, and later head number is a real empirical test and is what the cited experiment reports. Those data are not an open, reanalyzable set. Calling the pattern a counterfactual memory does not add a measurement that a non-representational cause of the later anatomy would fail." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: In anatomically one-headed planarians, compare the bioelectric pattern and gene-expression profile with later head number after an experimental cut. A two-headed voltage pattern before injury, with ordinary anatomy and ordinary expression, that predicts two heads after the cut, would support a pattern that is not a readout of current anatomy; a voltage pattern that matches current head number would refute that dissociation." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Voltage images and expression comparisons are in the source paper's figures, not a public image and count matrix.", "Predicting the regenerative outcome is expected of any causal prepattern, with or without memory of a counterfactual target." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-13--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of levin-2023-glue-13 by Grok 4.7: 0.6" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.6"^^xsd:double ;
